# Doc_Bot Workspace Layout

Telegram live-support bot (Go). **No frontend, no REST API, no migration tool** — webhook + SQLite only.

> **Note:** README lists `internal/app`, `internal/handlers`, etc. The **actual** tree is under `internal/config/`. Follow the real paths below, not the README.

## Top-level

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `cmd/bot/main.go` | Entry point: load `.env`, `config.MustLoad()`, `app.MustNew()`, `Run()` |
| `internal/config/` | All application code (config, wiring, handlers, service, storage) |
| `go.mod` / `go.sum` | Module `tg-bot`, Go 1.25+ |
| `.env.example` | Required env vars template |
| `README.md` | Product docs (architecture section is outdated) |
| `LICENSE` | MIT |

## `internal/config/` layers

```
internal/config/
├── config.go          # Env → Config struct (MustLoad)
├── app/app.go         # Wire bot + DB + service + handlers; webhook HTTP server
├── handlers/          # Telegram update routing (no business logic)
├── service/           # SupportService — forum topics, forwarding, UI cards
└── storage/           # SQLiteStore — schema init + SQL queries
```

### Handlers (`internal/config/handlers/`)

- `handlers.go` — `HandleUpdate`: callback vs message; manager forum vs private user
- `user.go` — `/start`, `/lang`, private messages → service
- `callback.go` — inline buttons (`lang:RU|UA|EN`)
- `texts.go` — user-facing copy + `sendText` / `sendLangMenu` helpers

### Service (`internal/config/service/`)

- `service.go` — `SupportService` struct + constructor
- `flow_user.go` / `flow_manager.go` — USER→managers and MANAGER→user message flows
- `user.go`, `pinned_card.go`, `ui_lang.go`, `lang_menu.go`, `start_hint.go` — focused features
- `helpers.go` — lang normalization, media extraction, Telegram error helpers

### Storage (`internal/config/storage/`)

- `store.go` — `OpenSQLite`, `Init()` (creates `users` table)
- `models.go` — `User` struct only
- `users.go` — user/profile/thread/pinned/status queries
- `messages.go` — `messages` table schema + `SaveMessage` / `ListMessagesByUser`

## Where things live

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Backend | Entire repo (`cmd/` + `internal/config/`) |
| Frontend | **None** |
| Database | SQLite file at `DB_PATH`; schema in `storage/store.go` + `storage/messages.go` |
| Config / secrets | `.env` (local), `internal/config/config.go`, `.env.example` |
| Tests | **None yet** — add `*_test.go` next to the package under test |

## Where to add new files

| Change | Put it here |
|--------|-------------|
| New bot command or callback | `handlers/` (+ wire in existing router) |
| New support flow / Telegram logic | `service/` (new file or extend `flow_*.go`) |
| New table or query | `storage/` (`models.go` for structs, dedicated `*.go` per table) |
| New env variable | `config.go`, `.env.example`, README if user-facing |
| New startup wiring | `app/app.go` |
| Tests | Same package, `foo_test.go` |

Keep **one concern per file** (existing pattern: `flow_user.go`, `pinned_card.go`, etc.).

## Do not touch without asking

- **`.env`** — contains `BOT_TOKEN` and secrets
- **`*.db`** (e.g. `docdata_bot.db`, `support.db`) — local runtime data
- **`cmd/bot/bot`** — compiled binary; rebuild with `go build`, do not edit
- **`.DS_Store`** — macOS metadata
- **Restructuring `internal/config/` → `internal/handlers`** to match README — large breaking refactor
- **Switching webhook ↔ long polling** — deployment-critical
- **Schema changes on live DBs** — no migration framework; coordinate manual/backfill steps
